Done. `FlattenOneof` now strips via `StripProto`, and `StripAndFlatten` combines both for create inputs.

```5:36:sdks/typescript/sandbox/src/oneof_input.ts
export type FlattenOneof<T extends ProtoOneof> = Simplify<{
  [K in Exclude<T["case"], undefined>]?: StripProto<
    Exclude<Extract<T, { case: K }>["value"], undefined>
  >;
}>;

export type StripAndFlatten<
  T,
  Oneofs extends {
    [K in keyof Oneofs]: K extends keyof T ? ProtoOneof : never;
  },
> = Simplify<
  Omit<StripProto<T>, keyof Oneofs & string> & {
    [K in keyof Oneofs & string]?: FlattenOneof<Oneofs[K]>;
  }
>;
```

`CreateOptionsInput` is derived from that (plus ms durations + plain `providerOptions`); `SandboxSourceInput` / `ReadinessProbeInput` come from its fields. Auth still uses `FlattenOneof` directly.

